  "conclusions": [
    "Semantic operations, geometric clipping, logical UPDATE, cursor hiding and Task handoff are distinct boundaries.",
    "The Atari timer gate skips supervisor-mode preemption; the AES trap offers scheduling after dispatch returns.",
    "An ordinary VDI return is not an automatic renderer handoff.",
    "One Exec physical grant can span multiple bounded device lists and overlay repair.",
    "GF14 rejected one larger-row candidate; source inspection does not prove an optimal row count."
  ],
